    {
      "title": "Native Drought-Tolerant Garden -- Design",
      "date": "2025",
      "type": "Design",
      "category": "planting",
      "notes": "A native, drought-tolerant planting for a Balwyn residence. A diverse palette of Australian-native grasses, shrubs and small trees is chosen for resilience to dry conditions and year-round interest, with a poolside softscape. Upper layer includes Elaeocarpus reticulatus and Waterhousia floribunda; mid layer Dodonaea viscosa, Correa alba, Westringia fruticosa and Westringia 'Wynyabbie Gem'; ground and edge layers Lomandra longifolia, Dianella caerulea, Chrysocephalum apiculatum, Stylidium armeria, Brachyscome Mauve Bliss and Hardenbergia violacea. Low maintenance once established."
    }
  ],
